From a816e51b3fb7a34fab2278ec10b26bf378fb955b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nigel Todman <veritas@vts-tech.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 05:28:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ui_scale: draw the in-game menus and status bars smaller
 (50-100 percent)

The menus and HUD are drawn into the fixed 320x200 canvas, so on a
modern display they occupy the same fraction of the screen as in
1993: the doom options menu runs all the way to the bottom edge of
the canvas and the status bar takes a third of the view height.

Add a "ui_scale" config key (percent, valid 50-100, default 100 =
pixel-identical with vanilla).  While a menu or the status-bar HUD
is drawn, the game drawers switch the scale on (V_UIScaleOn /
V_UIScaleOff in v_video.c) and the patch blitters draw the artwork
at pct percent of its original size with nearest-neighbour sampling:

- call sites keep their design coordinates, so every layout
  relationship is preserved exactly (sliders stay under their
  labels, widgets stay aligned inside the status bar, the FOV row
  still matches the other rows)
- doom/strife build the status bar in the unscaled 320x32 backing
  screen and blit it down in one go (V_CopyRectScaled); the rest of
  the band is cleared first so the shrunken bar leaves no stale rows
  or columns at the bottom/right edge
- heretic/hexen clear their status-bar bands the same way
- everything drawn through V_DrawPatch, V_DrawPatchDirect,
  V_DrawTLPatch, V_DrawXlaPatch, V_DrawAltTLPatch and
  V_DrawShadowedPatch follows the active scale; writes that would
  land outside the canvas are skipped (strife draws some patches
  partly off-screen by design)
- V_CopyRect scales while the UI scale is active, so the STLIB
  widget erases line up with the scaled bar
- the FOV row (M_DrawTextScaled) follows the active scale like the
  rest of the menu

The option is set in the setup tool (Display -> Advanced, spinner
50-100) or as "ui_scale" in the config file; 50, 75 and 100 give the
crispest results.  Messages, the automap and the 3D view are not
affected (they stay at 1:1 for now); at 100 the code paths are
bit-identical to vanilla.

Validation: 141 unit checks against the real v_video.c (sampling
matrices at 50/75, TL/XLA/ALTTL/SHADOW table ops, edge guards,
V_CopyRectScaled identity at pct=100, ambient routing through
V_CopyRect, layout budgets for all four games); full autotools build
of all four games + setup + server, zero warnings; the doom options
menu and status bar rendered from the real doom1.wad lumps at
100/75/50 and geometry-verified (35/19/9 percent canvas coverage,
bar edges exactly at the scaled coordinates, band black below and
right of the shrunken bar).
